# Build-time client env for Astro/Vite. Copy to .env.
#
# PUBLIC_API_URL does NOT belong here, even though it is a build-time value.
# The Cloudflare adapter pushes wrangler values and .dev.vars into process.env,
# and Astro reads env with an empty prefix, so Vite's final process.env pass
# outranks the .env files:
#
#   .dev.vars  >  wrangler.toml [vars]  >  process.env  >  .env
#
# Setting it here looks like it works and is then silently ignored — which is
# how a production build once shipped with http://localhost:8787 baked in.
#
# Set it where it is actually read:
#   local dev  -> .dev.vars             PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8787
#   production -> wrangler.toml [vars]  PUBLIC_API_URL = "https://api.example.com"
#
# `npm run deploy` parks .dev.vars for the build so the production value wins,
# and refuses to upload a bundle that still contains a loopback URL.
